Z||000052||kslish||02-03-2001||12:19 PM||||If you've got it narrowed down to purple or charcoal, I'd go with the charcoal like on the Viper's or maybe the newer Pontaic's.  Never really liked any of the purple Fieros I've seen at shows.  <P>I agree with you on the British Racing Green, I considered repainting my red Fiero that (thought it would be cool with the tan interior) but like you, once I saw one at a show it just didn't seem to work "right" on a Fiero (the same way I feel about purple).  <P>That Lotus Dark Blue (with some pearlcoat in it) may be an interesting option though....probably could get a nice deep show shine out of that.<P>However, since I know you are intending this to be a show car and surely an award winner like your last Fiero, I suggest a color that I haven't seen on many too many cars before and never on a Fiero.  Mitsubishi Durango Copper Pearl:<P> <IMG SRC="http://westpennfiero.onestop.net/images/eclips04.jpg"> <P>It was only available on 1995 Eclipses.  Here is a Camaro painted the same color:<P> <IMG SRC="http://westpennfiero.onestop.net/images/camaro1.jpg"> <P>It is easily orderable from a paint store (no special mixing needed) from PPG Paints.  I have always wanted to do a Fiero this color if I ever completely redo one from the ground up.<P>Ken S.<BR>'86 SC and '87 GT<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> <p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 02-03-2001).]||||reg||1
